Garden source diagnostic {"lines":["📖 LEARNED: Soft Step (Level 1). Move through woods like weather. Less noise, fewer surprises.","📖 Your old life taught you things. 2 skills from your past — check your Journal.","Nothing here looks like home. You know none of these plants. Learn fast.","📖 Your hands remember: knap a Stone knife (stone + vine) — the oldest tool there is. Find the stone.","📖 Your hands remember: weave cloth (3 plant fiber — strip it from cleared brush), and build a Water Filter (cloth + charcoal from fire ashes). Dirty water doesn't have to stay dirty.","You wake up with dirt in your mouth and blood on your hands that isn't yours. The sky is the wrong color — not sunset-wrong, wound-wrong. Zuri Perez. Chimney sweep. From Columbus, Ohio. That was yesterday. This is now. You have: Daughter's Drawing, Trail compass, Coat button, Notebook, Dispatcher's headset. That's everything you own in this world. Haven. Twelve people. The fire is lit. Last night, something walked past the treeline on two legs. Too tall. It stopped. It listened. Then it kept going. Nobody slept after that.","A woman, maybe 40s: \"We've got days of stores, not weeks. The treeline is the pantry now. Learn what's out there.\"","📓 Journal: Food won't come to Haven. Walk past the treeline — learn what grows out there, bring it back, and get it named at camp.","You tell the others you're heading out. Someone nods. \"Come back before dark.\"","— DAY 1 DAWN — The world wakes. Animals are active.","You push through the doors into open air. Haven grounds — tents, a fire pit, worn paths. The world is that way.","The pantry is in the hall. Your hands are not. (Light Fingers)","📖 LEARNED: Mediation (Level 2). Find the interest behind the position. They're not fighting about the thing — they're fighting about respect.","📖 Your old life taught you things. 1 skill from your past — check your Journal.","Nothing here looks like home. You know none of these plants. Learn fast.","📖 Your hands remember: knap a Stone knife (stone + vine) — the oldest tool there is. Find the stone.","📖 Your hands remember: weave cloth (3 plant fiber — strip it from cleared brush), and build a Water Filter (cloth + charcoal from fire ashes). Dirty water doesn't have to stay dirty.","You wake up with dirt in your mouth and blood on your hands that isn't yours. The sky is the wrong color — not sunset-wrong, wound-wrong. Marco Power. Lawyer. From Columbus, Ohio. That was yesterday. This is now. You have: Reading Glasses, Busker's harmonica, Trail compass, Wedding ring, Unnamed photograph. That's everything you own in this world. Haven. Twelve people. The fire is lit. They found a deer this morning. Inside out. Not eaten — unmade. Like something was trying to understand how it worked. It didn't finish.","A man, maybe 40s, with a nervous tic: \"Nothing grows here but dirt and tents. Past the treeline — that's where the green is. That's where the food is.\"","📓 Journal: Food won't come to Haven. Walk past the treeline — learn what grows out there, bring it back, and get it named at camp.","You tell the others you're heading out. Someone nods. \"Come back before dark.\"","— DAY 1 DAWN — The world wakes. Animals are active.","You push through the doors into open air. Haven grounds — tents, a fire pit, worn paths. The world is that way.","The pantry is in the hall. Your hands are not.","The pantry is in the hall. Your hands are not.","The pantry is in the hall. Your hands are not."],"inside":false,"tile":"haven","over":false}
